<title>CANADA: Foreigners buy Canada securities in January.</title>
<headline>Foreigners buy Canada securities in January.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign investors bought a net C$3.30 billion of Canadian securities in January, after buying a net C$3.29 billion in December, Statistics Canada said on Monday.</p>
<p>Canadian residents bought a net C$1.32 billion of foreign securities after buying C$3.71 billion in December.</p>
<p>Foreign investments in Canadian securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				 Jan	Dec</p>
<p>    Total		   +3.301   +3.287</p>
<p>    Bonds		   +1.099   +5.412</p>
<p>    Money mkt paper     +1.646   -2.814</p>
<p>    Stocks		  +0.556   +0.690</p>
<p>Canadian investment in foreign securities (blns of dollars):</p>
<p>				  Jan	Dec</p>
<p>    Total		   -1.317   -3.714</p>
<p>    Bonds		   -0.106   -1.284</p>
<p>    Stocks		  -1.211   -2.430</p>
<p>(A minus sign indicates more purchases from than sales of securities to non-residents, i.e. an outflow of money from Canada, Statistics Canada said.)</p>
<p>(For more information from Statistics Canada, contact Balance of Payments Division, Don Granger at 613-951-1864.)</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
